---
// Melbourne's Make Good Specialists section
// The image slot is a grey placeholder until Ali supplies a photo.
---

<section class="mg-specialists">
  <div class="mg-specialists__inner">
    <h2 class="mg-specialists__heading">Commercial Make Good Specialists<br /><span class="mg-specialists__accent">Melbourne</span></h2>
    <div class="mg-specialists__copy">
      We work with tenants, property managers and owners to restore commercial spaces to their original condition. One contractor. One quote. Every trade covered.
    </div>
    <div class="mg-specialists__split">
      <div class="mg-specialists__body">
        <p>
          A make good is the work a tenant must complete at lease end to return a space to the condition set out in the lease. For offices that usually means removing partitions and fitout, capping services, and repairing floors, walls and ceilings. For <a href="/services/make-good-solutions/warehouse-make-good/">warehouses</a> it often means racking removal, floor restoration and line marking.
        </p>
        <p>
          We inspect the site, review your lease obligations and give you a fixed price quote that covers every trade. A small office strip out can take 1 to 2 weeks and a large warehouse restoration 4 to 8 weeks, so the earlier you call, the easier it is to meet your handover date. Beyond lease end, we also deliver <a href="/services/remediation-solutions/">building remediation</a> and <a href="/services/roofing-solutions/">commercial roofing</a>. New to the process? Read our <a href="/learn/make-good-guide/">make good guide</a> or see <a href="/learn/our-process/">how a project runs from proposal to handover</a>.
        </p>
      </div>
      <div class="mg-specialists__media" role="img" aria-label="Image placeholder">
        <span>[Image to come: warehouse make good photo]</span>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<style>
  .mg-specialists {
    padding: 56px 24px 58px;
    text-align: center;
  }
  .mg-specialists__inner {
    max-width: 1120px;
    margin: 0 auto;
  }
  .mg-specialists__heading {
    margin: 0 0 18px;
    font-size: clamp(28px, 3.5vw, 40px);
    font-weight: 700;
    line-height: 1.25;
    letter-spacing: -0.01em;
    color: #ffffff;
  }
  .mg-specialists__accent {
    color: #F28C3A;
  }
  .mg-specialists__copy {
    max-width: 820px;
    font-size: 18px;
    line-height: 1.6;
    color: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.9);
    margin: 0 auto 32px;
  }
  .mg-specialists__split {
    display: grid;
    gap: 32px;
    align-items: center;
    text-align: left;
  }
  .mg-specialists__body p {
    font-size: 16px;
    line-height: 1.7;
    color: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.75);
    margin: 0 0 14px;
  }
  .mg-specialists__body a {
    color: #F28C3A;
    text-decoration: underline;
    text-underline-offset: 3px;
  }
  .mg-specialists__media {
    aspect-ratio: 4 / 3;
    width: 100%;
    border-radius: 8px;
    background: hsl(0 0% 32%);
    display: flex;
    align-items: center;
    justify-content: center;
    padding: 16px;
    text-align: center;
  }
  .mg-specialists__media span {
    font-size: 14px;
    color: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.6);
  }

  @media (min-width: 1024px) {
    .mg-specialists__split {
      grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr;
      gap: 48px;
    }
  }

  @media (max-width: 600px) {
    .mg-specialists {
      padding: 64px 16px 40px;
    }
    .mg-specialists__copy {
      font-size: 16px;
      margin-bottom: 24px;
    }
  }
</style>
